@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

title Sajha Auction - Auction Lifecycle (auctions.status)

[*] --> pending : Seller submits auction listing\nManageProduct::save()\nAuction updateOrCreate(status = 'pending')

pending --> pending : Seller edits listing before approval\n(approved products can no longer be edited)
pending --> [*] : Seller deletes unapproved product\nProducts::deleteProduct() (cascade)

pending --> active : Admin approves listing\nProduct::approveListing()\n(Products::approveProduct / ProductDetail::approveProduct)

state active {
  [*] --> Upcoming
  Upcoming --> Live : start_time reached\nAuction::isLive()

  Live --> Live : AuctionEngineService::processBid()\ncurrent_price and total_bids updated
  Live --> Extended : bid inside last timer_reset_seconds\nextended_end_time = now() + timer_reset_seconds
  Extended --> Extended : another late bid\n(deadline only ever moves later)

  Live --> AwaitingSettlement : effective_end_time passed\n(extended_end_time ?? end_time)
  Extended --> AwaitingSettlement : extended_end_time passed
}

note right of active
  Upcoming, Live, Extended and AwaitingSettlement are derived from
  start_time, end_time and extended_end_time.
  The stored status stays 'active' until settlement runs.
  Settlement is triggered by any of:
  - scheduler 'finalize-expired-auctions' (every minute)
  - AuctionDetail mount / render / placeBid
  All go through AuctionEngineService::checkAndFinalizeIfExpired()
end note

active --> completed : determineWinner()\nat least one bid_amount >= reserve_price\nwinner_id, winning_price, settlement_reason set
active --> ended_unsold : determineWinner()\nno bid_amount >= reserve_price\nwinner_id = null, winning_price = 0

completed --> completed : Order created for winner (status 'pending'),\nproduct.status = 'sold',\nAuctionWonNotification + AuctionWonMail\n+ NewOrderReceivedNotification to seller

note bottom of completed
  If the auction order is later cancelled
  (OrderCancellationService::cancel), the product returns to
  'active' but this auction row stays 'completed' as history.
end note

completed --> [*]
ended_unsold --> [*]

note bottom of ended_unsold
  Auction::isEnded() also lists an 'ended' status,
  but no code path ever writes it.
end note

@enduml
